course: dictionary
lesson: 2261
title: Words that sound like their meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the thing they describe. Say creaky out loud and it almost copies the noise of an old door opening. Words that copy a sound are sound words, and creaky is one of them.
explain: «Once kids hear the toilets are haunted, a dripping tap and a creaky door "prove" it.» The dripping tap and the door are both things that make noises, so creaky must mean making a squeaking sound. Check by swapping your meaning in: a squeaking door "proves" the ghost, and it still makes sense.
explain: Creaky can also mean old and not working as well as before, as in «creaky knees». When one word has more than one meaning, read the rest of the sentence. The word old in «a creaky old computer» is your clue.
fact: Creaky means making a long, high, squeaking sound when moved or stepped on.
fact: «Creaky floorboards» and «creaky stairs» build suspense in spooky stories.
fact: Creaky can also mean old and not working as well as before, as in «creaky joints» or «a creaky old computer».
fact: Creaky can describe a plan that is weak, out of date or not well put together.
fact: In science, creaking is a sound made by friction between wood or metal parts, and oil reduces it.
exercise: «A dripping tap and a creaky door "prove" the toilets are haunted.» What does creaky mean here? | Shiny and wet | Very cold to touch | *Making a squeaking sound when moved | Painted bright red
exercise: Grandpa says, «My creaky knees need a rest.» What does creaky mean? | *Old and not working as well as before | Making a squeaking sound | Full of water | Loud and happy
exercise: Lena says, «Their creaky plan will never work.» What does creaky suggest about the plan? | Strong and carefully checked | Very long and exciting | *Weak, out of date or not well put together | Painted in bright colours
test: Which sound does a creaky stair make when you step on it? | Loud bang | Soft hum | Silent glide | *Long, high squeak
test: What causes creaking in wood or metal parts, according to science? | *Friction between the parts | Cold water | Sunlight shining on them | Singing
exam: In «On the way down a swing turns height into speed, and the air and creaky chains slowly steal a little each time», what does creaky most likely describe? | Chains made of gold | Chains that glow in the dark | *Chains that squeak as they move | Chains the swing uses to climb
